{"records":[{"id":"xbx248k5ft","title":"DYRK1A-TGFβ Signaling Axis Determines Sensitivity to OXPHOS Inhibition in Hepatocellular Carcinoma","description":"Intervening in mitochondrial OXPHOS has emerged as a potential therapeutic strategy for certain types of cancers. Employing kinome-based CRISPR screen, we find that knockout of DYRK1A synergizes with OXPHOS inhibitor IACS-010759 in liver cancer cells. Targeting DYRK1A combined with OXPHOS inhibitors activates TGFβ signaling, which is crucial for OXPHOS inhibition-triggered cell death. Mechanistically, upregulation of glutamine transporter SLC1A5 transcription compensates for the increased glutamine requirement upon OXPHOS inhibition. DYRK1A directly phosphorylates SMAD3 Thr132, thereby suppressing the negative impact of TGFβ signaling on transcription of SLC1A5, leading to intrinsic resistance of liver cancer cells to OXPHOS inhibition. Moreover, we demonstrate the therapeutic efficacy of IACS-010759 in combination with DYRK1A inhibition in multiple liver cancer models, including xenograftes, patient-derived xenograftes and spontaneous tumor model. Our study elucidates how the DYRK1A-TGFβ signaling axis controls the response of tumor cells to OXPHOS inhibition and provides valuable insights into targeting OXPHOS for liver cancer therapy. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-12-13T15:22:10.239Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/xbx248k5ft","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/xbx248k5ft"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"ying","last_name":"cao","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Western Blot"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"ztg7pxr6ch","title":"STT3A is essential for Wnt signaling and represents a target for cancers driven by RNF43 deficiency","description":"This dataset contains the original raw and analyzed data supporting the manuscript “STT3A is essential for Wnt signaling and represents a target for cancers driven by RNF43 deficiency”. The study identifies STT3A as an essential regulator of the Wnt signaling pathway and a potential therapeutic target for RNF43-deficient cancers. Included data were generated from key experiments, including Wnt reporter assays (DDT), Western blotting (WB), and CRISPR screen, and other experiments central to the study","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2025-10-13T11:26:58.874Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/ztg7pxr6ch","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/ztg7pxr6ch"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Zhengjin","last_name":"He","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cell Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"hvfhwjtr7n","title":"TGM2-H3Q5ser-NNMT Axis Licences Stromal-Mediated Cancerous Growth","description":"This work provides new insights into how serotonylation signaling is translated into chromatin-based regulation within the tumor microenvironment and expands our understanding of how emerging histone modifications shape tumor-associated stromal cell states. We believe that these findings will be of broad interest to researchers in cancer biology, epigenetics, and immunotherapy, as they provide new insights into how histone modifications shape tumor microenvironment remodeling.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-07-08T17:27:28.131Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/hvfhwjtr7n","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/hvfhwjtr7n"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"yu","last_name":"zhang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Peiwei","last_name":"Chai","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cancer","Epigenetics"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"65pfcj4j4m","title":"Protocol of CRISPR-Cas9 knockout screens for identifying ferroptosis regulators","description":"Ferroptosis, an iron-dependent programmed cell death triggered by excessive lipid peroxidation, has shown promising therapeutic potentials in human diseases. Here, we describe a protocol of a CRISPR-Cas9 loss-of-function screen to identify regulators in response to different inducers of ferroptosis. We emphasize the steps of library amplification, drug treatment, high-throughput sequencing preparation, and bioinformatics analysis using Model-based Analysis of Genome-wide CRISPR-Cas9 Knockout (MAGeCK). We also present a method to discover the regulators of ferroptosis and verify the potential targets efficiently.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-10-24T01:46:48.793Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/65pfcj4j4m","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/65pfcj4j4m"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Xin","last_name":"Yang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Wei","last_name":"Gu","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["CRISPR/Cas9","Ferroptosis"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"b6555hx877","title":"PRRX2-Mediated Transcriptional Regulation of GLI2 Promotes Cell Proliferation, Invasion and Metastasis by Suppressing Cellular Senescence via Hedgehog Signaling in Pancreatic Cancer","description":"PRRX2-Mediated Transcriptional Regulation of GLI2 Promotes Cell Proliferation, Invasion and Metastasis by Suppressing Cellular Senescence via Hedgehog Signaling in Pancreatic Cancer","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-08-09T17:36:12.14Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/b6555hx877","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/b6555hx877"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jianxin","last_name":"Jiang","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cancer","Cancer Cell"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"xyv5tj2rcs","title":"EIF3D orchestrates the homeostasis of multiple signaling pathways governing the primed pluripotent stem cell identity","description":"Pluripotent stem cell identities such as differentiation and infinite proliferation have long been decoded in the frameworks of transcription factor networks, epigenomes, and signal transduction, yet unclear and fragmented. However, directing attention toward translation regulation, the bridge between these events promises to provide new insights into previously unexplained mechanisms. Functional CRISPR interference screening led to the discovery that EIF3D maintains primed pluripotency via selective translation regulation. The loss of EIF3D unbalanced the pluripotency-associated signaling pathways, disrupting primed pluripotency. Furthermore, we found that EIF3D safeguards robust proliferation by managing the translation of multiple p53 regulators that maintain low p53 activity in the undifferentiated state. Therefore, this study provides a paradigm for selective translation regulation that defines the primed pluripotent stem cell identity.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2023-11-30T14:04:26.679Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/xyv5tj2rcs","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/xyv5tj2rcs"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Kazutoshi","last_name":"Takahashi","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Numerical Analysis","Stem Cell","Flow Cytometry","Photograph"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"66ms37y66x","title":"Data for: A genome-wide CRISPR/Cas9 screen reveals that riboflavin regulates hydrogen peroxide entry into HAP1 cells  ","description":"CRISPR screen data for hydrogen peroxide mediated cell death","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2024-02-13T14:30:16.414Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/66ms37y66x","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/66ms37y66x"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"surachai","last_name":"supattapone","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Kenneth","last_name":"Mark","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Tamutenda","last_name":"Chidawanyika","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Oxidative Stress"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"b4wczz76gf","title":"Comprehensive mapping of key regulatory networks that drive oncogene expression","description":"Raw data deposit for manuscript \"Comprehensive mapping of key regulatory networks that drive oncogene expression\" including:\n1. CRISPR screen raw .fastq files\n2. Orignal gel images\n3. Raw datasets and statistics analysis for all bar plots\n4. TCGA datasets for plotting\nFor CRISPR screen raw read counts, MAGeCK processed comparisons and code deposit, please refer to the supplementary documents of the publication.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2020-11-16T17:38:30.826Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/b4wczz76gf","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/b4wczz76gf"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Lin","last_name":"Lin","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Big Data","Screening","Guide RNA","CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"f7btcr6x6d","title":"A non-canonical function of glutathione to suppress ferroptosis via FSP1","description":"Whole genome-wide CRISPR KO screen","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2026-10-02T11:41:52.925Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/f7btcr6x6d","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/f7btcr6x6d"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"BO","last_name":"CHU","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Cell Biology"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"8bck675bht","title":"Identification of ICAT as an APC inhibitor, revealing Wnt-dependent inhibition of APC-Axin interaction","description":"Adenomatous polyposis coli (APC) and Axin are core components of the beta-catenin destruction complex. How APC’s function is regulated and whether Wnt signaling influences the direct APC-Axin interaction to inhibit the beta-catenin destruction complex and not clear. Through a CRISPR screen of beta-catenin stability, we have identified ICAT, a polypeptide previously known to block beta-catenin-TCF interaction, as a natural inhibitor of APC.  ICAT blocks beta-catenin-APC interaction and prevents beta-catenin-mediated APC-Axin interaction, enhancing stabilization of beta-catenin in cells harboring truncated APC or stimulated with Wnt, but not in cells deprived of a Wnt signal. Using ICAT as a tool to disengage beta-catenin-mediated APC-Axin interaction, we demonstrate that Wnt quickly inhibits the direct interaction between APC and Axin. Our study highlights an important scaffolding function of beta-catenin in the assembly of the destruction complex and suggests Wnt-inhibited APC-Axin interaction as a novel mechanism of Wnt-dependent inhibition of the destruction complex.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2018-09-14T18:33:43.875Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/8bck675bht","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/8bck675bht"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Feng","last_name":"Cong","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Lei","last_name":"Ji","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Bo","last_name":"Lu","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Zhizhi","last_name":"Wang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Zinger","last_name":"Yang","orcid":null},{"first_name":"John","last_name":"Reece-Hoyes","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Carsten","last_name":"Russ","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Wenqing","last_name":"Xu","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Molecular Biology","Cell Biology"],"journal_issn":["10972765"]}],"total_records":140299,"page":1,"page_size":10,"execution_time":122,"aggregations":{"data_type_stats":{"dataset":140299,"collection":0},"access_type_stats":{"open":139544,"restricted":69,"embargoed":686},"top_funders_stats":[{"id":"https://ror.org/01h0zpd94","name":"Nat